Introduction to Drinking Water Treatment — TU Delft (@wu-delft: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_0XXF9PBVKKD6FWSJRVDTCKQXP4
TU Delft OpenCourseWare; course coordinator Luuk Rietveld. CTB3365DWx, published 4 February 2016, webpage revised 28 February 2023. [Complete public course](https://ocw.tudelft.nl/courses/introduction-to-drinking-water-treatment/).

Work the full progression through treatment schemes, water quality, groundwater and surface-water processes. Follow the available lectures and readings and attempt the dimensional and preliminary-design questions before consulting demonstrations. The overview groups the material into four modules; the navigation divides it into Drinking Water, Groundwater I–II and Surface Water I–II. Preserve this distinction when locating a reading.

The site lists a 56-hour study load and labels the programme Master, while the stated learning outcomes are introductory recognition and preliminary calculations. The course declares CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, subject to separate component notices. Public materials do not establish access to a live online laboratory, institutional assessment or every external text.

**Access checked 30 October 2026:** TU Delft announces replacement of this OCW platform at the end of 2026, with changed URLs and only partial course migration. The course page currently resolves and still states its licence. Retain permitted copies in a personal library with their notices and verify replacement links when needed; this repository keeps references only. MIT 1.85 and AguaClara provide alternative process readings linked in this trail.

**Return:** [Water and sanitation sources — complete books, methods and operating evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_7AMRJFFR11FF35KJM7Y7M05B3M).
